# Every tracked file is already LF in the index and CI runs on Linux, so give
# the working tree LF as well. Without this, core.autocrlf on a Windows checkout
# writes CRLF, and two things break: prettier --check fails on files CI itself
# formatted (.prettierrc.json pins endOfLine: lf), and `git add` prints a
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning that lint-staged folds into its own
# command output, so its backup step reads the warning as a revision and dies
# with "fatal: Needed a single revision" before prettier ever runs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Listed after the wildcard so it wins. These stay unconverted.
ROUTES/*.tsv -text
